%I A399659 #10 Oct 11 2026 22:41:16
%S A399659 1,1,2,4,8,18,38,87,192,440,998,2290,5272,12136,28150,65062,151474,
%T A399659 351442,819786,1908065,4456038,10396496,24300848,56795386,132852610,
%U A399659 310877688,727668738,1704196516,3991328120,9353198388,21916754100,51381073707,120448701730
%N A399659 Number of involutions of length n avoiding the patterns 4321 and 4231.
%C A399659 Equivalently, a(n) is the number of Motzkin paths of length n such that, for every pair of consecutive level steps, the number of down steps between them is at least the height of the first of the two (Barnabei, Castronuovo, Silimbani). The generating function satisfies a functional equation with one catalytic variable and can be expressed as an explicit continued fraction (see Formula). It is conjectured not to be D-finite.
%C A399659 Asymptotic analysis of the series by differential approximants suggests a non-D-finite generating function, with a simple pole at x = 1/mu1 and a subdominant pole at x = 1/mu2, where mu1 = 2.3482375627737 and mu2 = 2.1484. The coefficients behave as C1.mu1^n+C2.mu2^n, where C1=0.06917024 and C2=0.014 (_Anthony Guttmann_, private communication, Oct 2026).
%H A399659 M. Barnabei, N. Castronuovo, and M. Silimbani, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.39952">Involutions avoiding 4321 and another pattern of length four</a>, arXiv:2609.39952 [math.CO], 2026.
%H A399659 M. Barnabei, N. Castronuovo, and M. Silimbani, <a href="https://github.com/niccolo-castronuovo/involutions-4321">Companion code</a>, GitHub.
%F A399659 G.f.: (1 - q^2)/(1 - q - s - s^2*q^2/(B(1) - s^2*q^4/(B(2) - s^2*q^6/(B(3) - ...)))), where s = (1 - sqrt(1 - 4*x^2))/(2*x), q = s^2, and B(n) = (1 - q)^2 - s*q^n*(1 + q) (Barnabei, Castronuovo, Silimbani).
%e A399659 a(4) = 8: the involutions of length 4 are 1234, 1243, 1324, 1432, 2134, 2143, 3214, 3412, 4231 and 4321; all of them except 4231 and 4321 are counted.
%t A399659 nn = 31; s = Sum[CatalanNumber[k] x^(2 k + 1), {k, 0, nn}] + O[x]^(nn + 2); q = s^2; B[n_] := (1 - q)^2 - s q^n (1 + q); P = B[6]; Do[P = B[n] - s^2 q^(2 n + 2)/P, {n, 5, 1, -1}]; CoefficientList[Normal[(1 - q^2)/(1 - q - s - s^2 q^2/P)], x]
%o A399659 (Python)
%o A399659 def A(N):  # counts the corresponding Motzkin paths; state = (height, down steps still needed before a level step)
%o A399659     cur, out = {(0, 0): 1}, []
%o A399659     for n in range(N + 1):
%o A399659         out.append(sum(v for (h, r), v in cur.items() if h == 0))
%o A399659         nxt = {}
%o A399659         for (h, r), v in cur.items():
%o A399659             moves = [(h + 1, r)]
%o A399659             if h > 0: moves.append((h - 1, max(r - 1, 0)))
%o A399659             if r == 0: moves.append((h, h))
%o A399659             for m in moves: nxt[m] = nxt.get(m, 0) + v
%o A399659         cur = nxt
%o A399659     return out
%o A399659 print(A(32))
%Y A399659 Cf. A000085 (all involutions), A001006 (involutions avoiding 4321), A230556 (involutions avoiding 4231).
%K A399659 nonn
%O A399659 0,3
%A A399659 _Niccolò Castronuovo_, Oct 05 2026
